{"title":"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Answer_choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Answer choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solutions</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A license plate in a certain state consists of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> digits, not necessarily distinct, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> letters, also not necessarily distinct. These six characters may appear in any order, except that the two letters must appear next to each other. How many distinct license plates are possible? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/1/811203c133e3217b676c38601f926b0e9397952c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 10^4\\times 26^2\\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 10^3\\times 26^3\\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 5\\times 10^4\\times 26^2\\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 10^2\\times 26^4\\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 5\\times 10^3\\times 26^3\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"773\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d08114ee4db6dd8f480fb3434f3bc9cbb8595628.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\cdot10\\cdot10\\cdot10 = 10^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"161\" height=\"15\" /> ways to choose 4 digits.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/a/87a6a838ce4da87e07761ef4f3619b37d523b657.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$26 \\cdot 26 = 26^2$\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" /> ways to choose the 2 letters. \n</p><p>For the letters to be next to each other, they can be the 1st and 2nd, 2nd and 3rd, 3rd and 4th, 4th and 5th, or the 5th and 6th characters. \nSo, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/d/74dbf5a4d426fb8bb63d88ab4f21b351d2ee670c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 - 1 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> choices for the position of the letters.\n</p><p>Therefore, the number of distinct license plates is  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/3/543de661b5a80f03ebb0e9e0bd40f3d5fffc346b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\times 10^4\\times 26^2 \\Longrightarrow \\boxed{\\mathrm{C}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"170\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Answer_choices)\">Solution 2 (Answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/9/ed99f78014bdf57b62e04864d28c977b06fb23ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> ways to choose the digits and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/0/6300905274a14e3662f985359df57de52aaabb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$26^2$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> ways to choose the 2 letters. However, since the letters are next to each other, the result must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/d/afdbb3b27bc5dac8b7215aa2d866e2fc624e963a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^4\\cdot 26^2 \\cdot \\text{something}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"153\" height=\"20\" />. The only answer choice that matches this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/1/ff1cac0ec2caa1645f90b48b2827793673636a84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{C}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>~ Andrew2019\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/0W3VmFp55cM?t=847\">https://youtu.be/0W3VmFp55cM?t=847</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solutions\">Video Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/3MiGotKnC_U?t=1446\">https://youtu.be/3MiGotKnC_U?t=1446</a>\n</p><p>~ThePuzzlr\n</p><p><br />\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/f56aG55oG8w\">https://youtu.be/f56aG55oG8w</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A\">2006 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofprob